From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:50:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backport numpy 2 / modern scipy & scikit-learn compatibility

The 0.3.0 sdist on PyPI only supports numpy<2, scipy>=0.19.1 and
scikit-learn>=0.23.0, and still imports distutils (removed in Python
3.12). None of that builds or imports on the Python/numpy/scipy/
scikit-learn versions this registry ships for riscv64.

Upstream merged a fix for exactly this on main (not yet released, and
still reporting itself as "0.3.0dev0" in _version.py) that raises the
floor to numpy>=1.22.4, scipy>=1.13.1 and scikit-learn>=1.4.2,<2,
switches Cython extensions to the stable numpy 1.x-compatible C-API via
NPY_TARGET_VERSION, replaces distutils.version.LooseVersion with
packaging.version.Version, adopts the scikit-learn validate_data/
__sklearn_tags__ APIs through a small _compat shim, and updates a
handful of tests for pytest>=7 and scikit-learn's SGDClassifier
loss="log_loss" rename.

Carry those changes onto the 0.3.0 tag, leaving _version.py at "0.3.0"
since we are building the released version, not the upstream dev
snapshot. Also drop the accompanying [tool.cibuildwheel] i686 image
pin: cibuildwheel 4.x refuses to even validate the config with
manylinux-i686-image = "manylinux2010" set, failing every platform's
build, not just i686, which we never build here anyway.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/scikit-learn-contrib/scikit-learn-extra/commit/da55e27dbbc4c028874ab4f1e1057bd073480ba1]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
